-- A setter sees the getters as they were BEFORE the write that fired it (the engine's rule). A setter that reads a getter which depends on its own trigger property reads a stale value:
-- the loader refuses it and says what to do instead. Converted from tests/stale_setter.rs.

test a setter reading a getter of its own trigger is refused with the fix
PACK t 1
Light.shade getter: 'dark' if this.level < 3 else 'bright'
Light.level on-setter note:
  WHEN this.shade == 'bright':
    this.note = 'bright now'
error: stale

test the refusal names the getter the trigger and the fix
PACK t 1
Light.shade getter: 'dark' if this.level < 3 else 'bright'
Light.level on-setter note:
  WHEN this.shade == 'bright':
    this.note = 'bright now'
error: on-setter on Light.shade

test the refusal names the getter
PACK t 1
Light.shade getter: 'dark' if this.level < 3 else 'bright'
Light.level on-setter note:
  WHEN this.shade == 'bright':
    this.note = 'bright now'
error: Light.shade

test the dependency may run through other getters
PACK t 1
Light.a getter: this.level + 1
Light.b getter: this.a * 2
Light.level on-setter s:
  ALWAYS:
    this.out = this.b
error: Light.b

test acting from a setter on the getter itself is fine
PACK t 1
Light.shade getter: 'dark' if this.level < 3 else 'bright'
Light.shade on-setter note:
  WHEN this.shade == 'bright':
    this.note = 'bright now'
given Light:a {"level": 5}
exists Light:a

test a getter that does not read the trigger is fine
PACK t 1
Light.tint getter: str(this.hue) + '!'
Light.level on-setter s:
  WHEN this.tint == 'x!':
    this.note = 1
given Light:a {"hue": "x"}
exists Light:a

test a getter of another class is not this rule
PACK t 1
Lamp.shade getter: 'dark' if this.level < 3 else 'bright'
Light.level on-setter s:
  WHEN this.lamp == 1:
    this.note = 1
given Light:a {}
exists Light:a
